The issue `proxy isatty` suggests that when `rich.console.Console` attempts to check if its underlying file stream is a terminal using `isatty()`, it fails or behaves incorrectly when the file stream is wrapped by `rich.file_proxy.FileProxy`.

I observed that `rich/file_proxy.py` does not implement an `isatty()` method, which causes `rich/console.py` to return `False` (since `isatty` is `None`) when it should potentially be able to determine the terminal status correctly, or at least handle the proxy case gracefully.

The fix is to implement `isatty()` in `rich/file_proxy.py` by delegating the call to the underlying file object (`self.__file`).

I will modify `rich/file_proxy.py`.

